# Keeps the build context - and therefore the image itself - from ever
# containing the host's live runtime state or secrets. Without this, the
# Dockerfile's `COPY config ./config` bakes WHATEVER currently sits in
# config/ on the build machine (real Plex/Discord secrets in settings.json,
# activity history, dedupe/verify/archive state, resolve picks) directly
# into an image layer - harmless for the CI-built GHCR image (a fresh git
# checkout never has these gitignored files at all), but on TOWER, where
# docker-compose builds locally FROM the same directory these files are
# bind-mounted into at runtime, every `docker compose up -d --build` was
# silently snapshotting real secrets into a local image layer.
#
# Real incident this fixed: a container recreated before config/
# archive-state.json's bind-mount target was ever touch'd got an empty
# DIRECTORY there (the well-known bind-mount gotcha - see fileseed.ts's
# ensureSeeded). A build that ran while that directory still existed baked
# it into the image as a directory, permanently - so even after fixing the
# host-side path to a real file, the container refused to start at all
# ("mount ... not a directory") until the image was rebuilt. Excluding
# these paths from the build context entirely means COPY config ./config
# only ever ships the git-tracked events.json default, and the runtime
# bind mounts (plus each state module's own ensureSeeded) are the only
# thing that ever determines these files' real type/content - never the
# image.
config/settings.json
config/activity.json
config/dedupe-state.json
config/verify-state.json
config/match-overrides.json
config/archive-state.json
config/torrent-registry/

# Standard hygiene - large/irrelevant to what actually needs to reach the
# image, and no reason to send them to the Docker daemon as build context.
node_modules/
dist/
.git/
.DS_Store
.env
